<Footnotes>
  <li id="fn-sms-1">At 139 orders per hour with two bartenders, the bottleneck is hands pouring drinks, not the SMS stack. Each bartender is making a drink every fifty seconds, sustained, for an hour. The software's job is to never make them wait for a ticket and never let a runner pick up the wrong tray.</li>
  <li id="fn-sms-2">Cordova for the runner and KDS apps, picked because it shipped fast on the Android tablets we already had. There was never a good window for a rewrite, it was never the most important thing, and it never really got in the way of debugging or shipping. The textbook 2022 answer was React Native with a thin native printer module. The pragmatic one held up fine.</li>
</Footnotes>
